{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Patchset 2 (Gerrit 2230) — LLM-Review +1 on patchset 1; this patchset fixes the Verified -1.\n\nMY FIX WAS A REAL REGRESSION IN THE TEST HARNESS, and I want that recorded rather than\nsmoothed over. Adding the fetch-secrets call to the mcp blue-green path made 10 of the 16\ntests in tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_mcp_bluegreen.py fail: the fake box never provisioned a\nfetch-secrets.sh (it had no reason to — until this change the mcp path never called one), so\nevery simulated deploy aborted at mcp-secrets-fetch-failed before reaching its assertions.\n\nA subagent investigating this reported the failures as PRE-EXISTING, having 'verified' it by\nrestoring files from HEAD — but HEAD already contained my commit, so that check could not\nhave detected my own regression. I re-tested against origin/main directly: 15 of 16 passed\nthere. The failures were mine.\n\nFIX: the mcp fixtures now provision the same fetch-secrets.sh stub the bot-path fixtures\nalready use — the fake box modelling the real box, not an assertion being relaxed. Added\ntest_secrets_fetch_failure_aborts_before_touching_the_live_upstream, which pins the ordering\nthat makes the change safe: an SSM failure aborts while the OLD container is still serving.\nMutation-checked — removing the fetch-secrets call turns it RED.\n\nSide effect worth noting: this also unblocked the compose-parity test that the sibling\nstore-provisioning change needed, which had never been exercisable end-to-end in this\nenvironment for the same reason."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787715813119921001,"uuid":"629cee2f-b5a4-43f0-b677-e5e5f3320e0d"}